diff --git a/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-04-catalog-scope-uncertainty/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-04-catalog-scope-uncertainty/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f10df04c0d5f83eaa001a7a59624c756a629841a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-04-catalog-scope-uncertainty/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+## Why
+
+Real tender nomenclature includes consumables, water-treatment media and service-only work that the LD sellable-product catalog does not evidence. The current hybrid reranker is forced to choose between `MATCHED` and `NOT_FOUND` and is instructed to avoid `NOT_FOUND`, so unrelated catalog products can be presented for a request that should instead be handled as insufficient catalog evidence.
+
+Nearby retrieval rewrites, brand genericization, query-variant fusion, and product-span decomposition have been evaluated without a safe end-to-end gain. A narrowly affirmative scope signal is now the higher-information experiment, provided it fails open for ambiguous and product-bearing work lines.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add a deterministic classifier for a small, documented set of high-precision unsupported-request classes: filter consumables/media, water-treatment material or equipment, and service-only work.
+- Route only a request with affirmative unsupported-class evidence and no purchasable LD product-family cue to an ordinary `NOT_FOUND` result with the machine-readable reason `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE`; it must not claim catalog absence as fact.
+- Apply the route before hybrid retrieval/reranking and preserve current retrieval, canonicalization, reranking, result status, and candidate behavior for every non-routed query.
+- Add focused tests proving positive routing, required fail-open cases (including product-bearing service text and generic filters), result serialization, and no retriever/reranker invocation on a routed request.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `catalog-scope-uncertainty-routing`: Detects only affirmatively evidenced unsupported tender-request classes and returns an honest no-catalog-evidence result without suppressing plausible sellable-product matching.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected package code: a small pure request-scope classifier, `matcher.py`, result reason constants/types as needed, and `serialization.py` only if reason exposure needs adjustment.
+- Affected tests: focused classifier, matcher, and serialization tests using fakes; existing full test suite remains required.
+- No prompt, model provider, catalog/index representation, embedding, Qdrant, BM25 corpus, or index rebuild changes.
+- The public status remains `NOT_FOUND` for evaluator compatibility. `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` is deliberately a qualified reason, not a proof that no matching CSV row exists.

