+## 1. Scope classification
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add a pure request-scope classifier and shared `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` reason that recognizes only the combined-cue consumable/replacement-element, filtration-media, water-treatment, and service-only profiles defined by the spec; verify focused classifier tests cover each affirmative profile.
+- [ ] 1.2 Add fail-open classifier tests showing that a generic filter, unknown vendor/model, an action verb alone, and installation/repair text containing a concrete valve or fitting requirement return no scope decision.
+
+## 2. Hybrid result routing
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Invoke the classifier only at the normalized `match_one_hybrid_with_rerank` boundary and return an empty `NOT_FOUND` result carrying `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` for an affirmative decision; verify fake retriever and reranker call counts remain zero for that route.
+- [ ] 2.2 Preserve the existing hybrid path for every non-routed query, including raw-query canonicalization and reranking inputs; verify existing matcher canonicalization regression tests still pass.
+- [ ] 2.3 Verify the routed result serializes with no primary product or selected candidates and exposes `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` through the established debug reason without changing the non-debug payload shape.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run the focused scope-classifier, matcher, and serialization tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; verify all tests pass before handing the change to the outer evaluator.

