index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0c566ac9eaba5c4340cd52b008c195553b352e2b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-04-catalog-scope-uncertainty/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+## Context
+
+See `proposal.md` for motivation. The hybrid matcher currently always retrieves candidates and asks the reranker for `MATCHED` or `NOT_FOUND`; its prompt explicitly biases toward a reasonable compatible candidate. `MatchResult` already carries a nullable primary product and a reason that serialization exposes under debug. No main OpenSpec capability exists yet.
+
+The research corpus contains filter consumables/media, water-treatment requests, and work-only lines alongside product-bearing installation/repair lines. The fixed catalog has limited industrial filter coverage but no evidence for cartridge, ion-exchange, or water-treatment product classes. Therefore, lexical absence or an action word alone is not a safe route.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Add a deterministic, pure, high-precision scope decision before the hybrid matcher invokes retrieval.
+- Preserve evaluator-compatible `NOT_FOUND` status while distinguishing the qualified `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` reason.
+- Make the classifier and its fail-open boundary independently testable without live services.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Proving mathematical absence from the source CSV or declaring catalog coverage generally.
+- Identifying products, inferring an LD equivalent, changing retrieval/reranking, or broadening generic `filter` and work-action handling.
+- Altering dense-only or dense-rerank APIs in this bounded experiment; the production hybrid-with-rerank route is the target.
+
+## Decisions
+
+### Use a pure combined-cue classifier with explicit deny conditions
+
+Introduce a small request-scope module that normalizes whitespace/case and returns either `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE` or no decision. It will recognize only class profiles supported by the research: replacement/consumable filter parts or filtration media; water-treatment media/systems; and service-only work. Each profile needs multiple independent class cues rather than one vocabulary token.
+
+Before an affirmative decision, a product-family denylist blocks routing for concrete sellable LD families (for example valves, fittings, and catalog-style mechanical filter requests). Service action language and broad filter vocabulary are deny conditions only when the classifier otherwise lacks class-specific evidence. Unknown brands/models are ignored, not treated as absence evidence.
+
+This is preferred to a generic keyword blocklist because the latter would turn mixed work/product tender lines into wrong `NOT_FOUND`. Runtime catalog scans are rejected for this experiment: a hit/miss cannot establish technical compatibility, adds runtime work, and would make a high-precision scope decision depend on index availability.
+
+### Route only at the hybrid matcher boundary
+
+After the existing empty-query handling and normalized source query construction, `match_one_hybrid_with_rerank` asks the pure classifier for a reason. A returned reason creates `MatchResult(status="NOT_FOUND", reason="NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE")` with no candidates or selected product; otherwise control follows the current canonicalization, retrieval, and reranking flow unchanged.
+
+This is preferred to prompting DeepSeek with scope hints because prior selection/prompt interventions were unsafe and the provider cannot enforce a fail-open rule. A new `UNCERTAIN` status is deferred: existing evaluators, result models, scripts, and public contract recognize `MATCHED`/`NOT_FOUND`; the reason gives the required qualified semantics without conflating this experiment with a contract redesign.
+
+### Treat the reason as a stable machine-readable qualifier
+
+Define the reason once (rather than emitting prose) and preserve it through normal `MatchResult` serialization. The result must never contain an LD product, selected candidate, or fabricated compatibility explanation. Debug payloads already carry `reason`, so production payload shape does not expand in this change.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [A class profile catches a request with a viable LD product] → Require combined positive cues, deny routing when a sellable product family is present, and retain a fail-open default.
+- [The classifier becomes a catalog-absence assertion] → Name and document the result as `NO_CATALOG_EVIDENCE`; it reports scope evidence, not negative proof.
+- [A valid product request loses visibility because no retrieval occurs] → Keep the profile list narrow and test product-bearing service and generic filter counterexamples.
+- [The status does not express all uncertainty needs] → Preserve this as a scope experiment; a richer supported/plausible/insufficient result contract is a separate causal layer.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+1. Add the pure classifier and reason constant with focused unit coverage for each supported profile and its counterexamples.
+2. Integrate it in the hybrid-with-rerank boundary only, then add matcher and serialization tests with fake dependencies.
+3. Run focused tests and `python -m pytest -q`; the outer supervisor performs public/hidden evaluation and promotion.
+4. Roll back by removing the pre-retrieval call. No catalog data, index, provider configuration, or persisted state requires migration.
